From 293f996f493568be16dd0b54b6837477fef4977c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:18:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 070/249] Make the Liquid player background audio-reactive

Adds VisualizerAnalyzer: cheap, no-FFT bass/mid/treble/transient extraction fed from the equalizer's existing audio tap (EqualizerAudioProcessor), published as a throttled ~30Hz StateFlow rather than per-sample. Gated by a visualizerEnabled flag so the extra sample decoding only happens while something's actually consuming it - the EQ's bypass path otherwise stays a cheap bulk buffer copy.

LiquidBackground's blobs are nudged by the smoothed frame (bass swells radius, treble adds shimmer, a transient flashes) on top of the existing ambient drift rather than replacing it, behind a new 'Audio-reactive' switch in the player background settings (on by default, still respects power saver/paused same as before).
