Subject: [PATCH 075/249] Fix the rotary dials not responding, and the liquid
 visualiser rendering grey

- RotaryDial's drag handler closed over the value parameter directly, but detectDragGestures runs in a coroutine that survives across separate physical drags - so every drag after the first computed its delta against a stale value from whenever that coroutine started, not the value the previous drag actually landed on. Fixed with rememberUpdatedState on both the value and the callback.
- LiquidBackground rendered nothing (or effectively just the grey surface behind it) whenever cover-art palette extraction came back empty or dull/desaturated - the theme's own primary color now always fills one of the three blob slots, so there's a guaranteed vibrant color regardless of what the cover gives back.
- The audio-reactive frame was fed straight into the draw call at the analyzer's raw ~30Hz publish rate with no interpolation, which read as flicker rather than motion - now smoothed through animateFloatAsState before it reaches the renderer, and the beat-driven pulse/flash is a bit more pronounced so it's actually visible.
- Enlarged the rotary dials (56dp -> 76dp), their labels, the pull-down/panel handles, and the docked bottom transport's icons and padding.
