From 69cb001b2707f53c3d0ad0691d2017997d404702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:33:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 081/249] EQ color scheme rework, bigger handle, fix Liquid
 alpha-flash

- Sliders: track fill is always a fixed green, unfilled portion a
  light neutral (onSurface at low alpha) instead of a dim tint of the
  active color - decoupled from the dial/gradient settings entirely.
  Dial arcs keep following the value gradient or contrast color as
  before. All labels/value readouts now use the plain contrast color
  regardless of the gradient setting, for legibility - RotaryDial gets
  a separate textColor param so its arc and its text can differ.
  Sliders and their labels are now boxed in a subtle rounded-rect
  border. BandColumn's now-dead gradient plumbing removed.
- EqualizerPanelHandle enlarged from 64dp to 110dp, spanning most of
  the panel's header instead of a slim strip, with the grab pill and
  close button pinned to the top rather than centered; the gap before
  the scrollable content below it reduced to near zero.
- LiquidBackground: replaced the fixed-duration animation with a
  frame-accumulated clock whose rate scales with audio energy, and
  removed the alpha modulation tied to transients - the combination of
  a clock that never changed speed and brightness flashing on every
  transient was what read as "blinking" instead of flowing faster or
  slower.
