From c0d1d040a87954040c31570dd3df9f088be30e11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:36:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 089/249] Fix garbled unsynced lyrics, make Liquid's idle
 motion actually visible

Unsynced lyrics were joined with joinToString { "${it.first}\n" } -
the default ", " separator plus a manual trailing newline per element
produced "line one\n, line two\n, line three\n" instead of clean line
breaks, so any song whose lyrics come back unsynced rendered as a
garbled comma-joined blob regardless of the karaoke setting.

The Liquid petal shape's ambient wobble (present with no audio so the
shape is never static) only ever perturbed the outline around a fixed
centre point, at a small amplitude, under an 18dp blur - on a real
screen that reads as barely-there or fully static, "not moving" is a
reasonable thing to conclude by eye even though the clock was ticking.
Doubled the wobble/petal amplitude, added a slow drift of the centre
itself (same two-non-harmonic-sines trick SPHERES already uses) so the
whole shape visibly travels rather than only breathing in place, and
added a slow rotation of the petal pattern. Audio-reactive terms are
unchanged and layer on top exactly as before.
