From 4adc7df6cb83f68993ca3c6f0334adbce2cf7fb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:21:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 095/249] Fix Follow-theme's grey/black fallback, and a
 settings/behaviour mismatch

extractGradientColors() routed through Score.score(), which is tuned
for picking a good *theme seed* colour and filters out anything
low-chroma - near-grey, near-black, near-white. A lot of real album
art is exactly that (muted, sepia, black-and-white photography), so
this fell through to the hardcoded grey/near-black pair far more often
than the "genuinely colourless cover" case it was meant for, which is
what made FOLLOW_THEME read as "always black" regardless of the
playing song. Now ranks Palette's own swatches by population directly,
with no chroma filter - a background wash wants the two colours the
cover actually shows most, not two "good enough for a whole app theme"
ones.

Also: PlayerFrag's "Stop music on task clear" switch defaulted to off,
but MusicService.onTaskRemoved's own read of the same key defaults to
on - so the switch showed as off for anyone who had never touched it
while the app was actually behaving as if it were on. Matched the
switch's default to the one that's actually enforced.
