 text

The previous commit made the header box deliberately taller than the
image's own shape (HEADER_HEIGHT_BOOST), but the image stayed centred
in it - splitting the new extra height evenly above *and* below the
image instead of only above. That pulled the image's bottom edge away
from the artist-name text, which is pinned to the box's own bottom
edge: the name ended up floating over bare background with a visible
gap, instead of overlaying the photo's faded bottom the way it always
