From 0380c75489c5c04f4c54d89b77b5872689ec6a34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:24:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 125/249] Skip WEB_REMIX for 5 min after its stream is rejected
 for a video

MusicService's retry-on-source-error re-resolves from scratch, which
tries WEB_REMIX (MAIN_CLIENT) first again regardless of why the previous
attempt failed - if the rejection wasn't fixed by the accompanying
identity rotation, the one retry a song gets was spent repeating the
same failure instead of reaching a fallback client. Metrolist tracks
this per-video with a short TTL rather than a permanent skip, since the
rejection is often transient and WEB_REMIX is the only fallback with
premium formats/correct metadata.

PlaybackData/CachedStreamUrl now carry which client actually produced
the stream; onPlayerError records a WEB_REMIX-specific rejection before
retrying, and playerResponseForPlayback skips attempting WEB_REMIX's
stream (metadata is still fetched from it either way) while that record
is fresh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
