From a1f98aaf3b1da54147808e4f0ed6294ee73bf82b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:46:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 127/249] Download full-res thumbnails independently, fall back
 on load failure

Adds SongEntity.thumbnailPath (DB v21->22, additive nullable column) for
a downloaded full-res thumbnail kept in app-managed storage, entirely
independent of the song's own audio download - it survives deleting the
download and vice versa. DownloadUtil.downloadThumbnail/removeThumbnail
are the two operations, exposed as: an auto-download-with-song toggle
(DownloadThumbnailsKey, off by default) in Storage settings, and a
per-song "Download thumbnail"/"Remove thumbnail" menu action so it's
also usable one-off without downloading the song's audio at all.
SongEntity/MediaMetadata.getThumbnailModel() prefer the downloaded file
over any remote URL once one exists.

Also adds ArtworkFallbackToLowResKey: a Coil interceptor that retries a
failed high-res artwork request at a smaller size instead of showing
nothing, since the CDN occasionally rejects a very large size that
loads fine smaller.

