Subject: [PATCH 131/249] Put the real equalizer controls in Settings, not just
 its meta-settings

The Equalizer settings page previously only exposed the dials/contrast-
color/color-by-value toggles and profile management - the actual bands,
tone controls, and compressor still only existed inside the in-player
panel, unusable without an active playback session. Widened five of the
panel's composables (EqualizerCard, ToneControlsRow, CompressorSection,
BandColumn, BandEditor) plus quantizeTenth from private to internal and
mounted them a second time in the Settings screen, wired to the exact
same preference keys and update()/updateBand() logic the panel uses -
this is not a second implementation of the controls, just a second place
the same ones are mounted, so a change from either place is the same
change. Added the "Enable equalizer" master switch too, which previously
had no Settings-page home at all.

Also fixes an inaccurate doc comment on EqUseDialsKey found while wiring
this: the setting only affects the band editor's frequency/gain dials,
not the band-gain strip or bass/treble tone controls, both of which stay
fixed (sliders and dials respectively) regardless of it - ToneControlsRow
and BandColumn's own comments already said as much, but the preference
key's comment and this settings page's description text both overstated
its scope until now.

