From 5fd79fd79584835140e440ed75fc9d16f4a6bbd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:21:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 146/249] Never navigate to an artist with no real page

Every "view artist" action (the player's title-area link, its overflow
menu, song/album menus, both the plain and thumbnailed artist picker
dialogs) only ever checked "is there an id at all" before navigating. That's
true for a locally-generated placeholder id just as much as a real YTM
channel id - so tapping a song's only artist when that credit had no real
channel (a local file, or a combined "X & Y" credit that never resolved)
navigated to "artist/<generated-id>", a page with nothing real behind it.

Added MediaMetadata.Artist.hasArtistPage (mirrors ArtistEntity's own
isYouTubeArtist) and used it - or the existing isYouTubeArtist/plain id
check, per call site's artist type - to gate every one of these actions:
disabled/unclickable instead of navigating nowhere. Also dropped a redundant
duplicate clickable in ArtistDialog's plain-artist row that made its outer
Row's own click handler dead code.
