From 56ba5e06f97c6eaf0225531d9f0aa6dd3ed92ca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:21:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 147/249] Show an artist's videos as a song list when they have
 no songs of their own

An artist page's "Videos" carousel and its "Songs" list both come from the
exact same underlying data shape (a WatchEndpoint-backed item - see
ArtistPage.kt's fromMusicTwoRowItemRenderer/fromMusicResponsiveListItemRenderer),
distinguished only by whether an album got attached. That meant an artist
with videos but no proper songs rendered with nothing in the prominent song-
list position - just a video grid, styled like every other carousel.

Only kicks in when the artist genuinely has no Songs section of its own (one
that does takes priority, unchanged), and only for a section YTM itself
titled "Videos". New "Show artist videos as songs" switch under Library &
content > Display (default on) to opt out.
