Backup and Restore already covers every setting and the whole database
(including play counts/listen history) - it copies the settings DataStore
file and the whole song.db wholesale, not an enumerated list of keys, so
nothing new ever needed adding there. What it didn't have was a way to run
without the user manually tapping Backup and picking a destination each
time - SAF's file-picker launchers can't run unattended, so stats (and
everything else) only ever left app-private storage - wiped on uninstall -
when someone remembered to do it themselves.

