From 35fca1602a2a46ff1dd88ee609ac1d803291e460 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:37:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 162/249] Bound download stream requests the same way playback
 already is

DownloadUtil's data source never got the connection-duration/PoToken-
staleness defenses MusicService already has, and additionally appended a
"&range=0-<contentLength>" query param that tells googlevideo's CDN to
serve the entire file as one continuous transfer - guaranteeing a single
long-lived connection regardless of any HTTP-level chunking.

Ports the same three defenses from MusicService: bound every request to
MusicService.CHUNK_LENGTH via subrange() so the connection is periodically
re-established, cap the cached URL's trust window to
MusicService.STREAM_URL_TRUST_WINDOW_MS (40s) instead of YouTube's claimed
multi-hour expiry so a stale PoToken gets proactively re-minted, and add a
45s OkHttp callTimeout as a backstop. Drops the whole-file range query
param so it no longer fights the chunking.

