From 2884a2ecc03c4a8b79e08e74290bf6d4018f25d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:11:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 168/249] Fix Clear all downloads leaving DownloadManager's
 index stale

It called downloadCache.removeResource(key) directly for every cache
key, wiping the cached bytes and content metadata but never touching
DownloadManager's own persisted DownloadIndex or its live in-memory
download list - both of which kept believing every one of those
downloads was still STATE_COMPLETED. The next scan re-registered all of
them as "downloaded" from that stale index despite the cache being
empty, so:
- Tapping download again on one of them was a silent no-op:
  downloadSong() saw downloads.value[id] != null (from the stale
  completed record) and returned immediately.
- A genuinely new download request for the same id could race
  DownloadManager's now-inconsistent internal state and never resolve.

Switches to DownloadService.sendRemoveAllDownloads(context,
ExoDownloadService::class.java, false) - the same DownloadService entry
point sendAddDownload/sendResumeDownloads elsewhere in this app already
use - which removes each download properly: cache content, index, and
in-memory task together, leaving nothing stale behind.

