From f6837170d2f4ed6845330bfb4883f26315bc5d9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:26:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 170/249] Try VISIONOS before WEB_REMIX for streams, not just
 as a fallback

Keeps WEB_REMIX as MAIN_CLIENT (metadata, login-gated features - both
unaffected, since mainPlayerResponse is fetched unconditionally from
MAIN_CLIENT before this loop runs regardless of which client's stream
ends up used). But WEB_REMIX's stream was still tried first for actual
playback, which meant every song was exposed to its PoToken-staleness
failure mode (dying ~20-60s in) by default, only recovering via the
one-time source-error retry after it already happened once. Reorders
just the stream-client try sequence to [VISIONOS, WEB_REMIX, ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH, IOS]
- VISIONOS needs no PoToken at all, so trying it first avoids that
failure class for most playback instead of just recovering from it.

