Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:40:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 171/249] Raise the source-error retry cap from 1 to 5,
 matching yuuichi-s/OuterTune

Each retry only gets one more pass through the whole client try-order -
playerResponseForPlayback already cycles through VISIONOS, WEB_REMIX,
ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH, and IOS internally in a single call, breaking on the
first one that validates. Capping the retry itself at exactly one meant
that if the client that single retry happened to land on was itself only
transiently bad (not the original failing one, since WEB_REMIX gets
marked and skipped, but any of the others), the song just gave up
entirely - no third attempt to reach a different client or catch a fresh
VISIONOS resolve.

Ports yuuichi-s/OuterTune's own retry budget for this exact failure
class (theirs allows up to 5) instead of inventing a number. Switches
retriedAfterSourceError from a Set (present/absent) to a per-song retry
counter capped at the new MAX_SOURCE_ERROR_RETRIES constant.

