From 38c6ae3f6d9882cc200b20a286f96c7d02008ac1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:40:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 173/249] Refresh an existing artist's details on sync instead
 of only its like flag

The subscribed-artists sync inserted a full ArtistEntity for an artist it had
never seen, but for one that already existed it only ever touched
bookmarkedAt - the name, thumbnail and channelId the same request had just
fetched were thrown away. This is the one path that sees authoritative remote
values for a library artist, so an artist renamed upstream, or one first
created under a stale "- Topic" title by a build predating the dedup fix,
kept the old value indefinitely no matter how many times it re-synced. That
is the "older stale artists" half of the duplicate/stale artist reports; the
dedup on the song/album credit paths (insertOrHealArtist) was intact and is
untouched here.

Each field is only written when the remote actually supplied it and it
differs, and the row is only written at all if something changed, so this
doesn't churn lastUpdateTime on every sync for every artist.
