From 481368712d87969e55243d837e4213565980cc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:48:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 174/249] Fix ERROR_CODE_TIMEOUT (1003) I introduced in stream
 validation

Stream resolution runs inside a runBlocking that ExoPlayer's
ResolvingDataSource is waiting on, so every network round trip in the client
loop is latency the player is blocked for. Two changes in the previous commit
compounded there: widening the chain from four clients to six, and making
validateStatus fall back to a second probe when the deep-range one failed.
Worst case went from ~8 round trips to ~18, which was enough to blow the
player's own timeout before any stream got handed back.

validateStatus is now a single first-byte probe, matching what
yuuichi-s/OuterTune actually ships and verified on-device. Dropping the
deep-range pre-screen is not a loss: it was my own addition, it can only ever
guess at whether continuation requests will be refused, and the 403/410
recovery in MusicService.onPlayerError already handles that case properly
when it really happens - at zero cost until it does. Also took the
reference's skip-validation-for-the-last-client optimization: with nothing
left to fall back to, a rejection there would only discard the one URL still
on the table.

Worst case is now 11 round trips, and one round trip in the normal case where
the first client works.
---
