From 55daf0c3060c5ca21e8ef1439f60e20f976304f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:42:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 176/249] Keep WEB_REMIX reachable for streams, but only as the
 true last resort

Refines the previous commit, which cut WEB_REMIX out of the stream chain
entirely. Excluding it outright trades one failure mode for another: if
VISIONOS and both ANDROID_VR builds are all refused, there'd be no stream at
all, and silence is worse than a track that needs a mid-song re-resolve.

It now sits last in the chain, so it can only ever win a stream when every
client above it has already failed - and because it is last it also skips
validation, and because it is MAIN_CLIENT its response is the one already
fetched for metadata, so reaching it costs no additional request at all. It
remains the metadata client either way; that never depended on this list.

Worst case per resolution is now 3 player POSTs and 3 validation probes,
against ~18 two commits ago.
