From 514fcbe37003bfe6601bb0b507fb265cdb48d251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:18:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 178/249] Restore two more v0.18.2 behaviours, and log every
 client rejection at warn

Comparing the restored chain against Core-v0.18.2 line by line turned up two
things the interim rewrites had dropped:

- The WEB_REMIX stream-failure skip. The original recorded a WEB_REMIX stream
  rejection and skipped WEB_REMIX's stream on the next resolve for a short
  TTL, so the source-error retry reached a fallback instead of repeating the
  same failure. I had stubbed the tracking out to a no-op when WEB_REMIX was
  briefly excluded from the chain; with it back at position -1 the skip
  matters again. Restored as it was, TTL included.

- Validation depth. The original probed past the first chunk (PROBE_OFFSET)
  specifically to catch URLs whose continuation requests are refused - the
  start-clean-then-die-at-the-chunk-boundary failure. I had replaced it with a
  first-byte probe while chasing the timeout, but the timeout came from making
  *two* probes per client, not from the depth of one. Back to the original
  single deep probe, with one narrow addition: 416 counts as a pass, since it
  means the track is simply shorter than the probe offset rather than the URL
  being refused.

Also closed a diagnostic gap: a client turned away by playabilityStatus (bot
check, region block, age gate) only logged at debug, which is invisible in a
release build - so "why didn't this client win?" had no answer in the logcat.
Every rejection path in the loop now logs at warn or error with its reason.
