From b86ce3b2df95cababa2f5e8a251f5cd6d1437f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:25:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 180/249] Send each client's player request to the host that
 client actually lives on

Ported from MetrolistGroup/innertubex, whose extraction is the one known to
work for these clients. It routes the player endpoint per client -
music.youtube.com for the music clients, www.youtube.com for everything else -
and this codebase sent every client to music.youtube.com unconditionally.

That mismatch is visible in the logs: ANDROID_VR's player POST to
music.youtube.com came back as Google's network-level abuse page ("your
computer or network may be sending automated queries"), not a per-video
rejection. An Oculus VR app asking music.youtube.com for a player response is
a client/host pairing that doesn't occur in the wild, so anti-abuse treats it
as automation - and every fallback in the chain was making exactly that
request, which is why they all failed and why the throttle kept deepening.

- YouTubeClient gains useMusicPlayerEndpoint. WEB_REMIX and the VISIONOS
  builds set it (they genuinely present as music clients); the device clients
  don't, so their player requests now go to www.youtube.com with matching
  Origin/Referer, and the SAPISIDHASH is hashed against whichever origin the
  request is actually going to rather than always the music one.
