From 1ec9f5a6c8041af7e965676c453daa121cf583bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:36:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 187/249] Stop the artist thumbnail refresh re-triggering
 itself and hammering YouTube

The refresh loop collected the artist list and, for every artist missing a
thumbnail or older than 10 days, fetched its page and wrote the result back.
Writing back re-emitted the Room flow, which re-ran the whole collect body -
so on a large library each successful update restarted the pass and re-walked
everything still outstanding.

Worse, an artist whose fetch *failed* keeps thumbnailUrl null, which is the
very condition selecting it, so it was re-requested on every subsequent
emission indefinitely - an unbounded background request loop for any artist
that can't be fetched at all. Given we have spent this session chasing
YouTube's "automated queries" throttle, a loop quietly issuing repeat requests
for as long as the screen is open is worth removing on its own merits.

Now: the flow is mapped to just the set of stale artist ids and
distinctUntilChanged, so unrelated writes to the artist table (a like, a
rename, this loop's own update) don't restart anything; collectLatest replaces
collect so a genuine change abandons the old pass rather than overlapping;
ids already attempted this session are skipped, so a failure gets another
chance next launch rather than every few seconds; and requests are spaced,
since this is background housekeeping nobody is waiting on.
