From 3e76e20fda02080a3c3a31633bf9625c37475a34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:30:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 192/249] Revert the PoToken orientation swap - it was wrong,
 and measurably so

The previous swap put the video-bound token on the stream url and the
session-bound one in the player request, on the strength of a constant
name in Metrolist's PlaybackClientCatalog (PoTokenBinding.VIDEO_ID on
webGvsRequired). That read the rule off a name instead of the behaviour,
and it is wrong: googlevideo refuses such a url outright, answering the
very first 256KB range probe with a 403. Eight of eight resolves in a
release build failed with "stream validation failed: HTTP 403", where
the previous orientation passed validation every time.

Restores the original, which is also the scheme yt-dlp documents: the
stream url's GVS token is session-bound, the player request's token is
video-bound. Documented in place now, with the failure signature, so the
next person to wonder can rule it out in one log line instead of a build.

Also reverts the visitorData/dataSyncId comment to match what was
measured: binding the session token to dataSyncId when signed in changed
nothing - the url still failed at the same point - so the identity was
never the problem and visitorData stays, matching Metrolist.

Keeps the retry-order change and the VISIONOS PoToken removal from the
same series; neither is implicated, and the retry-order fix is what
stopped the chain exhausting itself into a bot-challenge error.
