From 7a607b9b06499714dc3a9e01b769df169e2ca127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:02:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 198/249] Follow the stream from fetch to playback and match
 Metrolist's handling

Compared this app's audio path against Metrolist's, since theirs works on
the same account and device. Four differences, all of them faults here.

Cancellation was being swallowed. MetrolistStreamResolver caught
Exception, which includes CancellationException, so when the player
abandoned a load the interrupt was logged as a failed extraction and the
caller carried on into its own client loop inside an already cancelled
scope. Every client there failed instantly - six of them inside ten
milliseconds, spaced 2ms apart where a real request takes about 100 - and
an abandoned load was reported as an unplayable track. It now rethrows,
and the client loop checks for cancellation before each attempt instead
of sweeping a dead scope.

A 45s callTimeout on both stream clients. OkHttp's callTimeout covers the
whole call including reading the body, so on a download it is a hard cap
on transfer time: anything not finished in 45s was aborted mid-file, and
once Media3's retries were spent the file stayed truncated. It was added
to force a reconnect before a "connection-duration cutoff confirmed at
roughly a minute" that does not exist - what failed at about a minute was
the number of small bounded range requests, not the age of the
connection. Metrolist sets no timeouts on its stream client.

The range shape now travels with the url on PlaybackData and
CachedStreamUrl rather than being recomputed at the fetch site, and comes
from innertubex directly when innertubex resolved the stream, so a future
change to its rules arrives with the library instead of needing to be
noticed and mirrored here.

withResolvedStream replaces the two hand-rolled fetch sites and matches
Metrolist's semantics on three details this had wrong: request headers
are merged rather than replaced, a bounded range starts at 0 rather than
at uriPositionOffset, and a bound never exceeds a length the caller
actually asked for.

Verified by assembling coreRelease.
---
 .../dd3boh/outertune/playback/DownloadUtil.kt | 23 +++---
 .../dd3boh/outertune/playback/MusicService.kt | 72 +++++++++++--------
 .../utils/MetrolistStreamResolver.kt          | 15 ++++
 .../outertune/utils/StreamRangePolicy.kt      | 11 ---
 .../dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt   | 20 ++++++
 5 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/playback/DownloadUtil.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/playback/DownloadUtil.kt
index ef12ba9d..0d8bf759 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/playback/DownloadUtil.kt
