From ba6c25848abe519b057cd03c17ff9220500aa5cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:37:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 210/249] Show a release's name rather than its tag in the
 updater

This repo tags releases by flavour and names them by version - the tag is
Core-v0.18.2 where the name is v0.18.2 - and the updater was reading the
tag. "New release available - Core-v0.18.2" reads as though the flavour
were part of the version number.

The name is used first now, with the tag as a fallback for a release that
has none. Both are only labels: what an upgrade is actually decided on is
the versionCode parsed off the end of the asset filename, which is
unaffected either way.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

