From 21f952075802e8ef99f6e1f14aee02ea69dae219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:27:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 215/249] Stop stripTopicSuffix turning a "- Topic" channel
 into a nameless artist

YouTube produces auto-generated channels titled exactly "- Topic", for
artists whose name came through empty on its side. That title matches the
suffix pattern in its entirety, so stripping it left an empty string, and
every caller of this stores or displays what it returns. The result was a
real artist row with no name: a credit that renders as blank, sorts
nowhere, and still links off to the junk channel it came from. On the song
that surfaced this, the credits read "Jasmine Clarke" and nothing.

Stripping is meant to tidy a name, never to remove it, so a strip that
would leave nothing is no longer applied. "- Topic" is a poor name to
show, but it is a name, and it is the truth about where that credit
points - unlike a blank, which reads as though the data were missing
rather than wrong. Fixed at the function itself rather than at any one
caller, since all six sites store the result.

That stops new ones. Rows already written keep their empty name, so the
enricher now drops a nameless credit when it meets one. There is nothing
to preserve by keeping it, and a song left with no credits at all picks
up its album's on the next pass, which is a better answer than a blank.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

