From 56bdd922a08ce925f14b8c2b93838354d579b3e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 10:54:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 218/249] Colour the EQ bands by value, drop the contrast
 switch, use UK spelling

The twelve band sliders were the one control in the panel that ignored
colour-by-value. Bass, treble, balance and every compressor dial took
their colour from it while the bands stayed a fixed green, which made the
setting look broken rather than deliberate - they are the controls most
obviously "a value within a range", so they are where it is expected to
show. Their track and thumb follow it now; the label above stays the
plain contrast colour, as every other slider's does.

Removed the "Use cover contrast colour" switch. The panel's cards are a
flat dark grey whatever the artwork is, so both of its positions looked
near enough identical, and a toggle whose effect cannot be seen is worse
than not having one. The panel is fixed to the theme colour, which is the
position it was being left in.

The same preference also coloured the equalizer handle on the player
screen, and there it is kept - unconditionally. That handle sits directly
on the cover art rather than on a grey card, which is exactly where
measuring a colour against the artwork earns its keep, so it keeps what
the switch defaulted to rather than what it was being turned off to get.

Also converted the user-visible American spellings to UK: colour,
favourite, behaviour, customise, centre, personalise. Resource names are
left alone - they are identifiers, and renaming them would break every
translation that references them for no visible gain.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

