From d0592da91cfc5bb2b9ee51117c5006ca93e61820 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:31:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 224/249] Normalise artist ids where they are stored, and
 relink on refresh

This is why the credits kept resetting. The enricher was fixing them one
song at a time on playback, and the ordinary library sync was undoing it
across the library: DatabaseDao and AlbumsDao store an artist id exactly
as YTM hands it over, and YTM hands the same channel over under two
spellings. Correcting the symptom on play was never going to hold while
the cause ran on every sync.

So the id is normalised at each of the six places a credit is written -
song artists, album artists, and the maps that join them. The prefixed
spelling now cannot enter the database at all, which is what makes a link
stay linked rather than survive until the next sync.

That leaves rows already stored, which is what the pull-to-refresh sweep
is for. relinkAll repairs every song whose stored rows show either fault -
an MPLA-spelled id, or a credit with no name - and it finds them with a
query against those rows rather than walking the library, since both
faults are visible in the data.

It runs at the end of the songs sync rather than on a schedule of its
own, so it happens immediately after the thing that would have caused the
damage. Offline only: the searching parts of enrich cost one request per
name, and firing those across a whole library for a refresh gesture would
be disproportionate. They still run per song on playback, where a single
request is fair.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

