From fc2f6af7e2e69189d88094df60e4f3fd3c46d80b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:05:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 225/249] Repoint a credit whose channel is an empty Topic
 channel

Confirmed against YouTube rather than inferred. The channel feed for the
id credited on those songs reads:

  UCPOtcixkNLHOLUZa_fG-ZPw   title=' - Topic'
  UC1t4kA0IZjtMeaLtApNZZug   title='Jasmine Clarke - Topic'

So the Seraphine credit carries a real, valid channel id that is
nonetheless a dead end: an auto-generated Topic channel whose artist name
came through empty on YouTube's side, holding nothing. The song still
names the artist correctly, because the name comes from the credit run
and not from the channel - which is exactly why this reads right and
opens nothing, and why none of the earlier fixes touched it. They were
all about names, and the name was never wrong.

Searching the name finds the channel YouTube itself answers with, which
is the populated one, since resolveArtist already requires a non-blank
thumbnail and a bare Topic channel has none. When that comes back as a
different id, the credit is repointed to it.

Gated on the stored artist having no thumbnail, which keeps it from
costing a request per credit forever: anything that has been through here,
or whose page has been opened, has a picture and is skipped. The gate also
selects the right candidates by construction, since an artist row built
from a credit run alone starts without one. The repointed row is stored
with the picture the search already returned, so the gate closes behind
it.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
