From 6d3c26a0b1d2db353816b5a5dc57dbc7c0e21854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:42:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 231/249] Stop the artist "view all" screen re-requesting the
 page it is already loading

The screen drives pagination from a snapshotFlow on the scroll position,
and it has two of them - one for the list layout, one for the grid - so a
single scroll to the end could call loadMore twice over. Worse, the flow
keeps emitting while the request is in flight, and the continuation token
only changes once the response lands, so every one of those emissions asked
for the exact same page again. The duplicates were invisible because
distinctBy swallowed them, but they were real requests competing for the
connection with the one that mattered, on a screen whose whole wait is the
network.

An in-flight flag is enough; the token itself is unchanged.

This does not make the first load faster. That is one browse request to
YouTube and the latency is theirs - the items are fetched fresh rather than
carried over from the shelf the arrow was tapped on, which would be the
real fix for the initial wait and is a larger change.

Verified by compiling coreRelease.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
