From 15acb00f7f4257759579485e210bc89efc5357c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:02:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 232/249] Add a search button to long playlists, behind a
 threshold

Scrolling a few hundred songs to find one is the problem; a playlist of six
does not have it. So the button appears in the header action row, next to
edit/sync/download/queue, only once a playlist is long enough to warrant
it - 50 songs by default, configurable in Library settings, or never.

It opens the search that already lives in the top app bar rather than
introducing one of its own. A second search field in the header would mean
two implementations of the same thing and a text box wedged into a row of
icons; this is a second way in to the same search, and the field appears
where it always has.

Local playlists only. Online and auto playlists have the top bar search but
not this action row, and edit/sync only exist for local ones anyway.

