From 232e51a3e07b80d72b75b57de6b49c680810290e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@l>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:29:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 238/249] Always request artwork at the size it will be drawn,
 and drop the setting

YouTube hands out whatever thumbnail suited the response it came from -
often 60-226px in browse and library payloads - and with this off those
went to Coil verbatim and were upscaled to fill the view, which is why
album covers looked soft.

The only thing the setting bought back was the difference between a small
JPEG and a slightly larger one, which is not a saving worth a soft cover on
every screen of a music app. So it is not a choice any more.

The low-res fallback stays, and keeps its toggle. It covers the CDN
refusing a large size outright, which is a fallback for a failure rather
than a preference about quality - it no longer depends on another setting
being on, so its enabled-state gate is gone too.

Verified by compiling coreRelease, and by grepping for the key, the mirror
field and both strings to confirm nothing still refers to them.

