From 7e2c6dd7919a5c87e99c2a864e9914820db85d14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: inspect <inspect@local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:28:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 242/249] Never let a stale local placeholder win over a real
 artist id

artistByNameIgnoreCase matches by name alone, with no filter on whether
the row it finds is an actual YouTube channel or a locally-generated
placeholder (a combined "X & Y" credit, an unresolved featured-artist
mention). Four call sites picked whatever that lookup returned over a
credit's own id without checking which kind it was:

- ArtistCreditEnricher.resolveArtistEntity, after confirming via search
  that a real, populated channel exists for a name, would still hand
  back an old placeholder sharing that name instead - discarding the
  very confirmation it just got and crediting the song to the same
  untappable placeholder this function exists to replace.
- The three artistByNameIgnoreCase call sites in DatabaseDao (song sync,
  album insert, album update) had the identical gap in the regular sync
  path, not just the enricher's special-case resolution: a placeholder
  left over from an earlier unresolved credit could override a real
  channel id the very credit being synced already carried.

Added String?.isRealArtistId() (db/ArtistTopicSuffix.kt) as the one
place that prefix list lives - ArtistEntity.isYouTubeArtist now
delegates to it too, rather than keeping its own copy that could drift.
Every fixed call site now prefers a real id from either side (the
existing row's, or the incoming credit's) and only ever falls back to
reusing an existing placeholder - to dedup placeholders sharing a name,
not to override a real one - when neither side has a real id at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
